ect"}, "input": {"path": "CHANGELOG.md"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The advisory says versions below 2.9.4 are affected, and 2.9.4 is the fix in the 2.x line. I'll pick 2.9.4 rather than 3.1.0 because it's a patch-level bump and avoids a major-version jump. Next I'll create the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01G3yen1QBkdDNsxSMk4R9xo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014txA3sx2yqn9B9o8Qrp6zq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "message": "Upgrade fastjson to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337\n\nVersions before 2.9.4 are vulnerable to unbounded recursion when parsing\ndeeply nested arrays. 2.9.4 contains the fix.", "files": [{"path": "requirements.txt", "content": "fastjson==2.9.4\nrequests==2.32.3\n"}, {"path": "CHANGELOG.md", "content": "# Changelog\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- Upgrade fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337 (unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays).\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed. Now I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019eJyy7pS5gHtyjx4S3vHcC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "idempotency_key": "fastjson-2.9.4-6c69ace862"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01F5RbCdDWKv5F8bq4uMxo9y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request alex as reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XdUGbwBMyknMsfcgTTYpMP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\n- Upgrades fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 in `requirements.txt`.\n- Adds a CHANGELOG entry under Unreleased.\n\n## Why\nCVE-2026-31337 (high): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affected versions are <2.9.4 and >=3.0.0 <3.1.0. 2.9.4 is the fix in the 2.x line, so this is a patch-level bump. I did not move to 3.1.0 because that is a major-version change.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `6c69ace862`: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-2.9.4-6c69ace862"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 and opened pull request #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Version choice:** CVE-2026-31337 affects versions below 2.9.4 and the 3.0.0 range. I chose 2.9.4 because it is the fix in the 2.x line and a patch-level bump. 3.1.0 is also fixed, but it is a major-version change.\n- **Branch:** `fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, with `requirements.txt` changed and a CHANGELOG entry added under Unreleased.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` on commit `6c69ace862` passed.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}